/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7300 — Item-page right-rail sticky top offset.
   csfloat's main nav is 70px tall and sticky at top:0 with bg rgb(21,23,28).
   Their item rail clears the nav by 10px, sticking at top:80px. Our rail
   was already at 80px in the 2026-05-02 scaffold but lost the value to a
   later override. Pin it explicitly to match the measured 70px nav + 10px
   gap, with a scroll-margin so anchor jumps land below the nav too. */
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2) {
  top: 80px !important;
  scroll-margin-top: 80px !important;
}
@media (max-width: 1100px) {
  body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2) {
    position: static !important;
    top: auto !important;
  }
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7300 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7301 — Right-rail max-height calculation.
   csfloat sets the rail max-height to viewport - (nav 70px + 24px breathing
   room) = calc(100vh - 94px). Our 100px value shaved 6px more than needed
   and the rail bottom didn't sit flush with the viewport floor on tall
   listings. Tighten to 94px, match csfloat exactly. */
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2) {
  max-height: calc(100vh - 94px) !important;
  overflow-y: auto !important;
  overflow-x: hidden !important;
  /* csfloat-style overscroll containment so wheel events don't escape the
     rail to the page once the rail bottoms out */
  overscroll-behavior: contain !important;
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7301 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7302 — Scroll-fade gradient at top + bottom of
   the right rail. csfloat overlays a 24px linear-gradient at each edge of
   the scrolling container so content appears to "fade" rather than hard-
   cut at the clip line. We approximate with mask-image: a vertical mask
   that's transparent for the first/last 18px and opaque in the middle.
   This is purely visual — no JS scroll listeners — and degrades to a hard
   edge in old engines that don't support mask-image. */
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2) {
  -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(
    to bottom,
    transparent 0,
    rgb(0, 0, 0) 18px,
    rgb(0, 0, 0) calc(100% - 18px),
    transparent 100%
  ) !important;
  mask-image: linear-gradient(
    to bottom,
    transparent 0,
    rgb(0, 0, 0) 18px,
    rgb(0, 0, 0) calc(100% - 18px),
    transparent 100%
  ) !important;
  -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat !important;
  mask-repeat: no-repeat !important;
  -webkit-mask-size: 100% 100% !important;
  mask-size: 100% 100% !important;
}
@media (max-width: 1100px) {
  /* On narrow viewports the rail collapses to a static block — kill the
     mask so the bottom of the section doesn't fade. */
  body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2) {
    -webkit-mask-image: none !important;
    mask-image: none !important;
  }
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7302 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7303 — Right-rail thin scrollbar polish to
   match csfloat exactly. csfloat uses a 6px-wide thumb in rgba(255,255,
   255,0.18) with a 0.32 hover state, transparent track. Our existing rule
   used --line-2 which is too dark on the rail's bg. Lock to the exact
   rgba mix csfloat ships, with subtle hover lift. */
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2)::-webkit-scrollbar {
  width: 6px !important;
  height: 6px !important;
}
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2)::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
  background: transparent !important;
}
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2)::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18) !important;
  border-radius: 3px !important;
  transition: background 140ms ease !important;
}
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2)::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.32) !important;
}
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2) {
  scrollbar-width: thin !important;
  scrollbar-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18) transparent !important;
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7303 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7304 — Sticky rail "stick point" on long pages.
   csfloat lets the rail run with the page until the user has scrolled past
   the page header (~24px), then clamps it to top:80px. With our sticky
   rail living inside a 2-row grid where the rail spans both rows
   (`grid-row: 1 / span 99`), the rail's natural top is the same as the
   image's top — so it sticks immediately on first scroll, which can feel
   abrupt next to the slow-scrolling listing column.

   Fix: add a small margin-top: 0 + an explicit `align-self: start` (already
   there) and use `contain: layout` on the rail so its sticky context is the
   grid track, not the page. This keeps the rail anchored to the same
   y-coord as the preview image until the user scrolls past, matching
   csfloat's "stick point". Also: `will-change: transform` on the rail to
   keep paints GPU-composited during sticky transition (no jank on long
   listing tables). */
body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2) {
  align-self: start !important;
  contain: layout !important;
  will-change: transform !important;
  /* Bottom padding so the bottom-edge mask doesn't clip the last actionable
     row — the user always sees a 12px breathing gap below the last item. */
  padding-bottom: 12px !important;
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  body main.modal.item-page > .modal-header > div:nth-child(2) {
    will-change: auto !important;
  }
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #7304 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #6805 — Home rotating card stack: lock .card-1/.card-2/.card-3
   intrinsic widths and heights to csfloat's measured values. csfloat ships:
   .card-1 width:265px height:279.453px (drawn 283x263 after 33deg 3D rotate),
   .card-2 width:265px height:414.359px (drawn 304x390),
   .card-3 width:265px height:468.562px (drawn 313x440). Without these locks the
   intrinsic SVG aspect ratio drifts and the back-card peek widths shift by ~12-18px,
   breaking the staircase. Position absolute on card-1/2 with top/left 0 so the .cards
   parent's translateX(-30px) is the sole anchor; card-3 stays static so it sets
   the .cards box height (472.562px). */
html body .image-container .cards .card-1 {
  width: 265px !important;
  height: 279.453px !important;
  position: absolute !important;
  top: 0 !important;
  left: 0 !important;
  z-index: 3 !important;
  transform-origin: 132.5px 139.727px !important;
  filter: drop-shadow(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3) 21px 21px 35px) !important;
}
html body .image-container .cards .card-2 {
  width: 265px !important;
  height: 414.359px !important;
  position: absolute !important;
  top: 0 !important;
  left: 0 !important;
  z-index: 2 !important;
  transform-origin: 132.5px 207.18px !important;
  filter: drop-shadow(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3) 21px 21px 35px) !important;
}
html body .image-container .cards .card-3 {
  width: 265px !important;
  height: 468.562px !important;
  position: static !important;
  z-index: 1 !important;
  transform-origin: 132.5px 234.281px !important;
  filter: drop-shadow(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3) 21px 21px 35px) !important;
