   loads), match csfloat's surface-on-panel tonal contrast: panel is
   rgb(27,29,36) and a quiet skeleton block reads as rgba(255,255,255,0.06)
   over it (same 6% white wash csfloat uses on hairlines/inactive chips).
   Border-radius mirrors csfloat's mat-card child surfaces: 8px for blocks,
   4px for inline lines (Material's small radius). sbox previously had
   bg rgba(255,255,255,0.06) which is correct — keep it but pin via !important
   so downstream rules can't drift it. */
html body .skeleton,
html body .skeleton-card,
html body .skeleton-thumb,
html body .skeleton-line,
html body .skeleton-body,
html body [class*="skeleton-"]:not([class*="skeleton-loader-wrap"]) {
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06) !important;
  border-radius: 8px !important;
  display: block !important;
  position: relative !important;
  overflow: hidden !important;
  /* establish the base stack — shimmer overlay is added on the
     ::after pseudo in the next ship to keep the brand tint visible */
  color: transparent !important;
  user-select: none !important;
  pointer-events: none !important;
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #14100 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #14101 (skeleton — shimmer animation, csfloat-toned)
   measured: csfloat's mat-progress-bar uses a 2-second translate sweep at
   cubic-bezier(.4,0,.6,1) (Material indeterminate). For block skeletons we
   reproduce that cadence with a 200% gradient sweep: 1800ms is the
   Material-2 indeterminate buffer cycle; we keep linear timing for
   continuous motion (csfloat's progress bar uses ease-in-out for the bar
   itself but the buffer dots loop linearly). Highlight band uses
   rgba(255,255,255,0.12) — slightly brighter than the 0.06 base, matching
   csfloat's hover/active surface lifts. We layer via ::after so the base
   color stays visible at the gradient's transparent stops. */
@keyframes csfloat-skeleton-sweep {
  0% { transform: translateX(-100%); }
  100% { transform: translateX(100%); }
}
html body .skeleton::after,
html body .skeleton-card::after,
html body .skeleton-thumb::after,
html body .skeleton-line::after,
html body .skeleton-body::after,
html body [class*="skeleton-"]:not([class*="skeleton-loader-wrap"])::after {
  content: "" !important;
  position: absolute !important;
  inset: 0 !important;
  background-image: linear-gradient(
    90deg,
    rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 0%,
    rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12) 50%,
    rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 100%
  ) !important;
  background-repeat: no-repeat !important;
  background-size: 100% 100% !important;
  animation: csfloat-skeleton-sweep 1800ms linear infinite !important;
  pointer-events: none !important;
  /* defeat any inherited transform from base block */
  transform: translateX(-100%);
  will-change: transform !important;
}
/* Also kill the legacy gradient on the base element so we don't double-paint
   (sbox had `linear-gradient` on the element itself which conflicts with the
   ::after sweep) */
html body .skeleton,
html body .skeleton-card,
html body .skeleton-thumb,
html body .skeleton-line,
html body .skeleton-body,
html body [class*="skeleton-"]:not([class*="skeleton-loader-wrap"]) {
  background-image: none !important;
  animation: none !important;
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #14101 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #14102 (skeleton-card variant — item card placeholder)
   measured: csfloat item-card box is 227.5px wide x 394.625px tall on /search;
   the visual chrome is a mat-card raised — bg rgb(27,29,36), border-radius
   12px, no border, padding 0, internal layout has thumb area top + body.
   For sboxmarket's `.skeleton-card` we use 12px radius (matches mat-card),
   keep aspect proportional (sbox already sets height: 280px; respect that
   but allow auto when consumer sizes via inline style). Min-height ensures
   a placeholder isn't collapsed when consumer omits dimensions. */
html body .skeleton-card {
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06) !important;
  border-radius: 12px !important;
  min-height: 120px !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  /* don't force a fixed height — let consumer's inline width/height drive
     so a 227.5x394 csfloat-style card slot can be rendered verbatim */
}
/* When card is inside a grid that also paints chrome, drop the inner
   chrome to avoid stacking */
html body .skeleton-card.skeleton-card-flat {
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04) !important;
  border-radius: 8px !important;
}
/* END CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #14102 */

/* CSFLOAT-1:1 PARITY ship #14103 (skeleton-line variant — text placeholder)
   measured: csfloat's body text inside item-card is 13px line-height ~18px;
   FloatDB rows have 14px text @ line-height 20px. For text-line skeletons we
   want a band that reads as a single line: 12px tall is too thin (1.4mm@96dpi
   reads as a hairline) — Material's spec for text placeholders is .75em → on
   csfloat's 14px base that's 10.5px. Keep 12px (Sbox default) for now but
   pin border-radius to 4px (csfloat's small-radius token) and tighten margin
   to 6px so stacked lines match csfloat row-rhythm of 6px gaps. */
html body .skeleton-line {
  background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06) !important;
  border-radius: 4px !important;
  height: 12px !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  display: block !important;
