   2033-2087) which always emits class="stall-share-btn" and toggles
   visual state via title= and an inline `style={border, color}` prop:
       follow-not-yet  -> title="Get notified when this seller lists ..."
                         JSX inline style sets `var(--accent-border)` border
                         + `var(--accent)` text — currently a near-mono
                         ghost in the canvas. csfloat-equivalent for the
                         primary CTA is the mat-mdc-raised-button (golden
                         measure on csfloat homepage Sign-in button):
                           h40, padding 13px 30px, min-width 64px,
                           font-family Roboto, fs15, fw700, lh normal,
                           letter-spacing normal, text-transform none,
                           color rgb(255,255,255), bg rgb(35,123,255),
                           border 0, radius 8px,
                           transition box-shadow .28s cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),
                           shadow rgba(0,0,0,0.2) 0 3px 1px -2px,
                                  rgba(0,0,0,0.14) 0 2px 2px 0,
                                  rgba(0,0,0,0.12) 0 1px 5px 0.
       following       -> title="Click to unfollow"  JSX inline sets
                         `var(--border)` border + opacity .75 — currently
                         no brand affinity, no hover hint. csfloat outlined
                         primary measure (mat-mdc-stroked-button, .reset-btn
                         on toolbar reset row, golden measure):
                           h36, padding 0 15px, fs14, fw500, radius 8px,
                           1px solid hairline rgba(255,255,255,0.12),
                           transparent fill, color = primary brand,
                           transition border .28s cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1).
                         For the follow surface we keep csfloat's filled
                         h40 geometry across BOTH states (it's the seller-
                         hero CTA, not a row chip — a 4px state-driven
                         height shift would jitter the hero layout) but
                         flip the fill: filled-brand for "Follow",
                         transparent + 1px brand border for "Following".
   The lane needs the surface to override the inline style{} from the JSX
   so we lock everything with !important and target the title= attribute.
   APPEND-only; do not modify the token block at top.

   #19600 — base geometry / typography lockdown for both states. csfloat
   raised primary measured: h40, padding 13/30, fw700, fs15, radius 8px,
   min-width 64px, font Roboto, lh normal, color/bg overridden per state
   below. Locks display:inline-flex with 8px gap so the +/✓ glyph and
   trailing follower-count span align on the baseline. `box-sizing
   border-box` so the 1px border of the following-state doesn't push
   geometry +2px. Disabled state mirrors mdc-button disabled (cursor
   default + pointer-events none + opacity .5). */
.stall-share-btn[title*="Get notified"],
.stall-share-btn[title*="Click to unfollow"],
.stall-hero .follow-btn,
.stall-hero button.follow {
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
